;; Which picture is which, for each direction the player can face.
;;
;; :stand is the picture for standing, :walk a cycle of four. A picture is a
;; PNG's name (:player-03 is the file player-03.png), or [top bottom]: the top
;; half (the head and shoulders, the first 16 pixels down) of one PNG with
;; the bottom half (body and legs) of another, so a walking picture doesn't
;; need its own head. A name that isn't imported yet is drawn as the first
;; picture that is, so you can fill these in as you draw them.
;;
;; {:mirror :right} draws the direction as the other one, backwards, so
;; side-on art is only needed for one side.
;;
;; The PNGs: 01 stands facing us; 02 and 03 are steps facing right, and 04
;; stands facing right; 05 stands facing away, and 06 and 07 are steps facing
;; away. Facing us, the steps are made from our head with the legs of the
;; steps facing away.
{:down  {:stand :player-01
         :walk  [[:player-01 :player-06] :player-01 [:player-01 :player-07] :player-01]}
 :up    {:stand :player-05
         :walk  [:player-06 :player-05 :player-07 :player-05]}
 :right {:stand :player-04
         :walk  [:player-02 :player-04 :player-03 :player-04]}
 :left  {:mirror :right}}
